set.body:
Add the expression-level semantic foundation without introducing solver-specific operations as maps.

Deliverables:
- capability-preserving TypedMap hierarchy for linear, affine, smooth, and general maps;
- product expressions and multi-parameter targets;
- Functional traits for convexity, smoothness, homogeneity, separability, spectral structure, gradients, Hessian-vector products, conic form, and proximal availability;
- FeasibleSet traits for convexity, closedness, projection, conic form, manifold structure, normal cone, and separability;
- distinct PenaltyTerm and ConstraintTerm nodes;
- program symmetry inference from map equivariance plus functional/set invariance;
- result semantics derived from the intersection of base, penalty, and constraint symmetries.

Acceptance:
- construction and capability tests on JVM/JS;
- elementwise l1 versus row-group l21 produces frame-selecting versus subspace-preserving contracts;
- unsupported capabilities cannot be claimed without a consuming lowering;
- serialization and diagnostics preserve public penalty-versus-constraint intent.
